WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.040
Speaker 1: Today, we're going to be speaking
with former Republican congressman from Illinois,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.620
Joe Walsh, former presidential candidate,
host of the new podcast White Flag with Joe

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.620
Walsh.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.620
Really appreciate your time.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.389
Speaker 4: Hey David, I've been a fan of yours.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:16.560
It's good to be on with you, man.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.560
Speaker 1: Thank you.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.560
So OK.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.840
I mean, so to start to give the audience some
sense.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.150
I mean, in the Tea Party era, you were not
just a Republican.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:31.260
You were sort of like a leading voice in the
Tea Party movement, strong opponent of Barack

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.120
Obama.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.600
And then at some point during the Trump era,
things things started to change for you.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.370
Speaker 4: Yeah, yeah.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.210
That's a that's a gentle way of putting it,
David.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.210
You're right.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.350
Look, I was a tea party guy, a big tea party
leader.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.020
You would have called me a crazy tea party
back in the day.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.020
Yes.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.070
And you and I could have had some interesting
debates and fights about the Tea Party.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.899
But generally it was about issues.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:04.649
And then Trump came along, and now the Republican
Party, the party I belong to my whole life

00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:08.399
is basically an anti-democratic cult.

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:10.299
And I didn't want to belong to a cult.

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:13.869
It doesn't matter where you stand on the issues.

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:16.000
It's always been the issues that drove me.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.969
I don't recognize this party anymore.

00:01:17.969 --> 00:01:18.969
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:24.180
And what's interesting about that is when
I chart the path to Donald Trump of the Republican

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.779
Party.

00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:28.939
The Tea Party, in my mind, was a big piece
of that.

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:35.119
In other words, you now say, Well, the Tea
Party made sense to me, but Trump doesn't.

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:42.119
But if we go back to the civil rights era
and then Reagan Gingrich in '94, but the way

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:47.530
I've seen it is, all of this has been a move
by the Republican Party away from substance

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.189
and towards cultural issues and being anti-democratic.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:56.619
And it's interesting that I mean, do you agree
that the Tea Party in a way set the stage

00:01:56.619 --> 00:01:57.619
for Trump?

00:01:57.619 --> 00:01:58.619
Speaker 4: Absolutely.

00:01:58.619 --> 00:01:59.619
Oh, you do.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.619
Yeah.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:01.619
No, you're spot on.

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:07.310
And in fact, I've publicly apologized for
helping bring you and I and the whole country

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.310
Trump.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.819
What I did helped bring Trump.

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:12.980
I look at it like this, David.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.769
The the Republican Party base is mostly middle
aged, older white people.

00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:24.230
And for years and years, the party establishment
ignored them and their concerns.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:31.489
And then Tea Party people like me came along
and inflamed them and riled them up.

00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:39.069
And then by the time Trump came along in 16,
they were primed baby to be captivated by

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.120
a cult show to be captivated by a demagog.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.620
So I led to Trump.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.069
I think the Republican Party establishment
did as well.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.659
Speaker 1: When did you?

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:54.260
OK, so when Trump started to run?

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.909
What was your initial thought and how did
that evolve over time?

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.810
Speaker 4: David, I screwed up.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:03.769
I didn't pay enough attention to him when
Trump started running in 15 and 16.

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:09.159
I was on the radio, you know, right wing talk
radio, two hundred stations around the country,

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:11.489
but I never paid enough attention to him.

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:13.499
I didn't take him seriously.

00:03:13.499 --> 00:03:17.129
I voted for him in 16 because he wasn't Hillary.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.300
I figured he's just a goof.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.750
And maybe he'll play golf for four years and
nothing will happen.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.480
I thought, Excuse me, I messed up David.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.769
I messed up.

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:33.290
Once he got elected, I started to pay attention
to him and I realized every time he opened

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.189
his mouth, he told a lie.

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:36.920
I couldn't live with that.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.379
And then I began to see and really see all
the uglier things he did.

00:03:41.379 --> 00:03:47.680
My final straw, David, was Helsinki in the
summer of 2018, when he stood on that stage

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.030
and said, I'm with Putin and not the Americans.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.980
That was the greatest act of disloyalty I've
ever heard.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.560
I went on the radio that night and said, I'm
going to do everything I can to make sure

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.010
he's not reelected.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.349
I began to lose, then my radio show and everything
shortly thereafter.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:06.700
Speaker 1: So here's one of the things I'm
interested in because we earlier this week

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:11.599
we were reading about Republicans holding
closed door meetings to try to figure out

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:16.959
how can we get Trump's grip on the party loosened
and all of these things.

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:24.030
I've seen no evidence that those folks are
actually against the authoritarianism of Trump,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.030
it seems.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.230
They just don't like Trump at the head, but
that they're sort of OK with the authoritarianism

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.110
that has been ushered in by Trump.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.110
Where are you on that issue?

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.889
Like, is the problem just Trump?

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:41.120
Or is it the Trump ism that I mean, like DeSantis
to me, seems like it's the same sort of mold,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.259
for example.

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:46.820
Speaker 4: David, you and I agree, man, I
totally agree.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.590
Look, it Trump has metastasized.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.590
He unleashed it.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.350
It is now Trumpism.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:59.710
If Trump went away tomorrow, it'll be a dis
Santas or somebody like that who will who.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:07.110
It's a party now that has embraced authoritarianism,
that is this Republican Party.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:12.669
I don't want to be a part of that, so anybody
who stands against that no longer has a place

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:13.669
in this party.

00:05:13.669 --> 00:05:19.319
Speaker 1: So like when you I mean, in figuring
out your politics now, when you look at Joe

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:23.930
Biden, for example, like just to pick taxes,
I don't know to pick something right?

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:28.349
Joe Biden wants the top tax rate to go up
a couple points.

00:05:28.349 --> 00:05:33.660
And there are some on the right who want like
a 25 percent top tax rate or whatever when

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:39.840
you see the Trump and Biden differences on
taxes like on that policy issue.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.960
Where would you like to see the top tax rate?

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.300
Speaker 4: Well, I probably don't support
either one.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:51.009
You know, Trump's tax reform piece of legislation
that he passed right away, I thought, was

00:05:51.009 --> 00:05:56.530
a lousy piece of legislation because it did
lower taxes for wealthier Americans.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.539
David, I generally support the notion of a
flat tax.

00:06:00.539 --> 00:06:02.699
You do simplifying the tax code?

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:08.180
Yes, simplifying the tax code so that wealthier
Americans who got all the accountants and

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.180
the lawyers.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.570
I think most studies I've read, if you simplify
the code, wealthy people actually pay more.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:18.710
I prefer a route like that that I don't think
Biden or Trump support.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.030
Speaker 1: Well, I think so.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.030
OK?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:25.120
If you figure out the effective tax that's
being paid by the very rich and then you set

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.620
the flat tax above that and you say not only
is this the flat tax, it's also the minimum

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.440
tax so that you can't loophole and deduct
your way out of it.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.710
You could have a situation where the very
rich do pay more.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:40.340
I think the problem people would have then
is somebody making $40000 a year is paying

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:41.340
the same rate.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.940
Would you to dig a little deeper on this?

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.130
Have some threshold below which you pay no
federal tax?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.520
Or how do you deal with the regressive nature
of it?

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.889
Speaker 4: I think there's always going to
be some threshold where people at a certain

00:06:54.889 --> 00:06:57.069
