00:06:57.069 --> 00:07:02.180
I do believe, but I do believe generally David
and you and I might disagree on this.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:05.500
The notion of progressivity in a tax rate.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.800
I generally oppose really.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.120
I generally, yeah, I generally believe just
a flat rate.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:16.940
And and the more money you make, you're going
to pay more because you're making more money.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.479
But I don't believe you should have a higher
rate.

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:22.539
But David, what's fascinating to me is.

00:07:22.539 --> 00:07:25.889
I can't remember having this discussion in
the last five years.

00:07:25.889 --> 00:07:26.889
All right.

00:07:26.889 --> 00:07:33.189
Like, like actually talking about a substantive
policy issue, the Republican Party doesn't

00:07:33.189 --> 00:07:35.100
talk about stuff like this anymore.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:42.169
Speaker 1: So to that end, why would they
start going back to issues if it's not clear

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:44.360
