00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.480
Speaker 4: Well, you know, it's odd, David.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.480
I'm not.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.700
I'm not a moderate and no one would ever call
me a moderate.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:59.780
But generally the only national non Trump
Republicans are moderates like a Romney.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.080
Mm hmm.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:07.420
But there's no way on God's green earth Mitt
Romney or anybody like that could get a nomination

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.800
in this in this party.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.100
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:14.860
So I guess then the question becomes what
happens in in 2024?

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:19.010
And I think there's two questions if the question
is who has the best shot of winning?

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:22.920
I don't think it's anybody you would actually
like to see representing the party.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.920
If the question is what's what would be best
for the party and the country?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:28.920
I think you're right.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.090
There doesn't really seem to be an interest
in that type of Republican right now among

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.180
